====================================================================
QUESTION 1 : What is Git, and why do software development teams use it?
====================================================================

Interview Ready Answer

Git is a Distributed Version Control System (DVCS) used to track
changes in source code, maintain version history, and enable multiple
developers to collaborate efficiently on the same project.

Definition

Git is a Distributed Version Control System.

Purpose

• Tracks source code changes
• Maintains version history
• Enables team collaboration
• Supports parallel development using branches
• Restores previous project versions when required

Important Keywords

• Distributed
• Version Control
• Collaboration
• Commit History
• Source Code Management

Memory Trick

Git = Track + History + Collaboration

